      url: "https://doi.org/10.1590/1984-70332018v18n4a61",
      licence: "CC BY (SciELO)",
      cultivar: "40 populations of Type II to III parents; controls A525, Perola",
      conditions: "Field, Coimbra MG, Brazil, dry season; rows 0.5 m apart at 12 seeds per m (about 24 plants per m2); hypocotyl diameter by caliper 1 cm below the cotyledon node at physiological maturity: mean 4.76 mm, populations 4.31-5.40 mm (R1 numbers, research thread)",
    ),
    "burridge2016": Source(
      citation: "Burridge J., Jochua C.N., Bucksch A., Lynch J.P. (2016) Legume shovelomics: high-throughput phenotyping of common bean and cowpea root architecture in the field. Field Crops Research 192: 21-32.",
